WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.700
MARTIN OMANDER: Hi Dina.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.700
DINA PORTMAN: Hi Martin.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:03.537
How are you doing?

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:04.620
MARTIN OMANDER: Just fine.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.120
Thanks.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.210
What are we working on today?

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.730
DINA PORTMAN: Well,
my friend Holly

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.010
works for a large
marketing research firm.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.680
She uses a Cloud Function
to write to her Cloud SQL

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.662
database.

00:00:14.662 --> 00:00:16.079
She's concerned
that somebody will

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:20.230
find her HTTP Cloud Function
and access her database.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.150
MARTIN OMANDER: Aha.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.300
She should use an ingress
controlled function.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.250
That way, no one on
the public internet

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.870
can access the function.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.675
We can set it up with a virtual
private Cloud connector.

00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:33.852
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:40.492 --> 00:00:41.950
DINA PORTMAN: An
ingress controlled

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.597
function sounds great.

00:00:43.597 --> 00:00:46.180
The new product she's working
on is collecting flavor research

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.740
for a candy company.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.420
She has a Cloud
Run front end that

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.000
sends the vote data to
a Cloud Function which

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.230
parses and validates the data.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.590
Then it sends the data
to another Cloud Function

00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:00.580
called write_to_db which inserts
the row into the Cloud SQL

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.920
table.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.760
So here is the app.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.117
And we can vote for kale,
margarita, or watermelon.

00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:08.950
MARTIN OMANDER: Hmm.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.380
Kale lollipops, Dina?

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.660
Is this a California company?

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.450
DINA PORTMAN: I think so.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.670
MARTIN OMANDER: I think it
would be watermelon for me.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.212
DINA PORTMAN: Kale's winning.

00:01:22.212 --> 00:01:23.170
MARTIN OMANDER: Oh, no.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.340
DINA PORTMAN: [LAUGHTER]

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.620
Holly really wants
to ensure that there

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.220
are zero fraudulent rights to
her database in the future.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.503
How do we achieve this?

00:01:31.503 --> 00:01:33.670
MARTIN OMANDER: Well, she
should update the settings

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:38.890
on her write_to_db function to
only allow internal traffic.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.340
This will exclude any network
requests not originating

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.092
from the same project.

00:01:44.092 --> 00:01:44.800
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.220
So I have my Cloud
Function here.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.510
And I'm clicking edit.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.620
I scroll down.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.512
I see variables, networking,
and advanced settings.

00:01:57.512 --> 00:01:58.720
Is that where it's going to--

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:58.960
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:01:59.670
Networking.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:00.330
Yeah.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.038
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:01.600
Networking.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.110
And Advanced, Environment
Variables, or Connections?

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.620
MARTIN OMANDER: Internal.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.512
Set to internal traffic.

00:02:11.512 --> 00:02:12.220
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.178
Allow internal traffic.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:17.650
OK.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:18.457
Let's try voting.

00:02:18.457 --> 00:02:19.540
MARTIN OMANDER: All right.

00:02:22.078 --> 00:02:23.370
DINA PORTMAN: It's not working.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.380
It's a 500 error.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.070
MARTIN OMANDER:
That's actually good.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:29.670
That means that the network
settings are working.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.400
We updated the
function write_to_db

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.770
to only accept
private connections.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.980
But the function candy_vote
isn't sending its data

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.170
through a private connector.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:43.590
Now we need to ensure that
candy_vote is using a VPC

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.920
connector to call write_to_db.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.022
But first, you need to
create the VPC connector.

00:02:50.022 --> 00:02:50.730
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.000
Let's do it.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.870
So I'm in the VPC
network settings.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.140
I'm going to
Serverless VPC access.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.500
And I am clicking
create connector.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.600
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.610
DINA PORTMAN: Name,
candyvote-connector.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:08.950
That's pretty good.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.367
MARTIN OMANDER:
That sounds great.

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:11.520
DINA PORTMAN: Yeah?

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.257
Network, default?

00:03:14.257 --> 00:03:15.090
MARTIN OMANDER: Yep.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.792
Defaults are our friends here.

00:03:17.792 --> 00:03:18.750
DINA PORTMAN: IP range.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.130
I really don't know.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.945
But they give an example, so I'm
just going to use that example.

00:03:22.945 --> 00:03:23.820
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.290
Let's go with the default.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.410
DINA PORTMAN: OK, and create.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.725
I have a VPC connector.

00:03:29.725 --> 00:03:30.600
What do I do with it?

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.580
MARTIN OMANDER: Excellent.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.270
Now, you go and update
the candy_vote function

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.790
to use that VPC connector.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.010
This means that any
outgoing requests

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.560
from the candy_vote
function, like calls

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.330
to the write_to_db
function, they

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:48.230
will go through
the VPC connector.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.320
DINA PORTMAN: OK.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:54.390
So when I go in, and I
look at the connections.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.550
Right here, it says
Egress settings,

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.100
and then I select
candy-connector.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.170
Excellent.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.290
And route all traffic
through the VPC connector.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.530
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah, all of it.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.230
DINA PORTMAN: And I've deployed.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.520
Let's try voting again.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.020
MARTIN OMANDER: Yeah.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.329
DINA PORTMAN: What
should I vote for?

00:04:15.329 --> 00:04:17.079
MARTIN OMANDER: Maybe
margarita this time.

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:20.917
DINA PORTMAN: It works.

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:21.959
MARTIN OMANDER: Ah, good.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:25.535
Well, we need to gang
up on those kale people.

00:04:25.535 --> 00:04:28.430
If you wanted to make it
even a little more secure,

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:31.400
you could update the
Cloud SQL database

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.790
to be a private IP Cloud SQL.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.250
So currently, the
write_to_db function

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.960
only accepts internal traffic.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.240
But if we update
the outgoing request

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.670
to go through a
VPC connector, we

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:48.080
could connect to the
private IP Cloud SQL.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.240
What this means is
that even if somebody

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.190
has the SQL database
as root password,

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.535
they can't connect to it
from the public internet.

00:04:55.535 --> 00:04:58.160
DINA PORTMAN: That sounds like
a really good use of our network

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.597
settings.

00:04:59.597 --> 00:05:00.680
MARTIN OMANDER: Excellent.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.407
I can't wait for my favorite
new flavor of lollipop.

00:05:04.407 --> 00:05:05.990
DINA PORTMAN: I hope
the kale lollipop

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.290
counts towards my daily
servings of vegetables.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:12.640
[MUSIC PLAYING]

